# Supabase & Data Access

## Three clients — never mix them up
1. `createClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/server` — cookie session, RLS, Server Components + user APIs
2. `createClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/client` — browser auth only (`AuthForm`, sign out)
3. `createAdminClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/admin` — **SERVER ONLY**, service role, bypasses RLS

## When to use which
- Public product reads (ISR/SSG): cookie-less anon client inside `src/lib/products.ts` (`createStaticClient`)
- User profile updates: server `createClient()` — respects RLS
- Orders, admin mutations, uploads: `createAdminClient()` after `getAdminUser()` check

## Admin auth
- Always guard admin API routes with `getAdminUser()` from `@/lib/auth`
- Never import `createAdminClient` into any `"use client"` file

## Fallback mode
- If `isSupabaseConfigured()` is false, use `FALLBACK_*` from `@/lib/fallback-data`
- Return 503 from order API when Supabase/service role is missing

## DB types
- Keep `src/types/db.ts` aligned with `supabase/schema.sql`
- Snake_case in DB; camelCase only at API/form boundaries
